# Preflight guard writes this into the SITE repo's data/ at runtime; any copy here is a stray
# from running the guard with the root pointed at this repo (e.g. a --selftest). Never track it.
data/preflight-status.json

# Timestamped backups of gitignored secret-bearing files (2026-08-08).
# distribute/config.json is ignored because it holds live API keys, app passwords
# and OAuth tokens — but every script that edits it writes a config.json.bak-<ts>
# copy alongside, and those .bak files were NOT covered by that rule. A single
# `git add -A` swept five of them (devto.api_key, hashnode.api_key,
# bluesky.app_password, mastodon.access_token, pinterest.app_secret) into a commit.
# Caught before push; nothing reached the remote. An ignore rule on the ORIGINAL
# file is worthless if the tooling writes copies under a different name.
*.bak-*
*.bak
